Here is the exhaustive, execution-ordered reconstruction of the `POST /api/owners` create-owner path.

## Routing overview

- The endpoint is defined on the generated interface `OwnersApi` and implemented by `OwnerRestControllerV1`. There is a `v2` controller (`OwnerRestControllerV2`) but it only implements a paged *list* (`GET`), not create. The create handler is `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`.
- Full path: class-level `@RequestMapping("/api")` + interface `@RequestMapping(method=POST, value="/owners")` = `POST /api/owners`.

---

## 1. The @RestController method (and interface mapping)

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`

Class declaration (lines 66-69):
```java
@RestController
@CrossOrigin(exposedHeaders = "errors, content-type")
@RequestMapping("/api")
public class OwnerRestControllerV1 implements OwnersApi {
```

Handler (lines 173-217):
```java
@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")
@Override
public ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto) {
    ownerFieldsDto.setAddress(AddressNormalizer.normalize(ownerFieldsDto.getAddress()));
    validateRequiredFields(ownerFieldsDto);
    validatePostcode(ownerFieldsDto.getPostcode(), ownerFieldsDto.getCity());
    HttpHeaders headers = new HttpHeaders();
    Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto);
    owner.setTelephone(TelephoneNormalizer.normalize(owner.getTelephone()));
    owner.setEmail(normalizeEmail(owner.getEmail()));
    validateRegistrationDate(owner.getRegistrationDate());
    if (owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) {
        owner.setRegistrationDate(LocalDate.now());
    }
    owner.setRegistrationDate(toBusinessDay(owner.getRegistrationDate()));
    boolean sharesHousehold = Boolean.TRUE.equals(ownerFieldsDto.getSharesHousehold());
    owner.setHouseholdId(HouseholdNormalizer.householdId(owner.getLastName(), owner.getPostcode()));
    owner.setIdentityKey(buildIdentityKey(owner));
    if (!sharesHousehold) {
        rejectHouseholdDuplicate(owner.getHouseholdId());
    }
    Integer possibleDuplicateOf = sharesHousehold ? null : findPossibleDuplicate(owner);
    owner.setPossibleDuplicate(possibleDuplicateOf != null);
    owner.setPossibleDuplicateOf(possibleDuplicateOf);
    if (countOwnersInCity(owner.getCity()) >= CITY_OWNER_LIMIT) {
        throw new OwnerCityFullException(owner.getCity());
    }
    long ownersRegisteredOnDay = countOwnersRegisteredOn(owner.getRegistrationDate());
    if (ownersRegisteredOnDay >= DAILY_OWNER_LIMIT) {
        throw new OwnerDailyLimitException(owner.getRegistrationDate());
    }
    boolean bulkSignupWarning = ownersRegisteredOnDay > BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD;
    owner.setCustomerCode(buildCustomerCode(owner));
    owner.setNamesakeCount(countNamesakes(owner.getFirstName(), owner.getLastName()));
    owner.setHouseholdSize(countHouseholdMembers(owner.getHouseholdId()) + 1);
    this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);
    AUDIT.info("owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={} membershipLevel={}",
        owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate(),
        MembershipLevel.forOwner(owner));
    OwnerDto ownerDto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
    ownerDto.setBulkSignupWarning(bulkSignupWarning);
    headers.setLocation(UriComponentsBuilder.newInstance()
        .path("/api/owners/{id}").buildAndExpand(owner.getId()).toUri());
    return new ResponseEntity<>(ownerDto, headers, HttpStatus.CREATED);
}
```

The signature/annotations `@Valid @RequestBody`, HTTP method and path come from the generated interface. `/home/daniel/sandbox/target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/api/OwnersApi.java`:

- Interface is `@Validated` (line 44).
- Lines 79-87:
```java
@RequestMapping(
    method = RequestMethod.POST,
    value = OwnersApi.PATH_ADD_OWNER,          // "/owners"
    produces = { "application/json" },
    consumes = { "application/json" }
)
default ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(
    @Parameter(name = "OwnerFieldsDto", description = "The pet owner", required = true) @Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto
) { ... }
```

So the effective annotations on the concrete handler are: `@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")`, `@Override`, plus inherited `@RequestMapping(POST /owners)` and the parameter's `@Valid @RequestBody`, under a `@Validated` interface.

---

## 2. Request DTO and its Bean Validation annotations

`/home/daniel/sandbox/target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/dto/OwnerFieldsDto.java` — constraints are on the getters (validated because of `@Valid`):

- `firstName` (line 76): `@NotNull @Pattern(regexp = "^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$") @Size(min = 1, max = 30)`
- `lastName` (line 97): `@NotNull @Pattern(regexp = "^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$") @Size(min = 1, max = 30)`
- `address` (line 118): `@NotNull @Size(min = 1, max = 255)`
- `city` (line 139): `@NotNull @Size(min = 1, max = 80)`
- `telephone` (line 160): `@NotNull @Size(min = 1, max = 20)`
- `email` (line 181): `@Size(max = 255)` (optional)
- `postcode` (line 202): `@Pattern(regexp = "^[0-9]{4}$")` (optional)
- `registrationDate` (line 223): `@Valid` (LocalDate, optional)
- `birthDate` (line 244): `@Valid` (optional)
- `sharesHousehold` (line 265): no constraints; request-only Boolean, not persisted

These run **first**, before the handler body, via `@Valid`/`@Validated`. A violation throws `MethodArgumentNotValidException` → 400 (see section 5/handler advice).

Note: the DTO `@Pattern` for telephone is only `@Size`-bounded here; the E.164 shape is enforced later in code (section 3). Also note the target entity `Owner`/`Person` carry their own Bean Validation annotations, but those are **not** triggered on this path (see section 6).

---

## 3. Service layer + all in-handler validation/transformation (in execution order)

After bean validation passes, the handler executes in this exact order. Helper methods are all in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:

1. **Address normalization** (line 176) — `AddressNormalizer.normalize(...)`, mutates the DTO before required-field check.
   `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/AddressNormalizer.java` (lines 47-64): trim, collapse whitespace, uppercase, expand whole words `ST→STREET`, `RD→ROAD`, `AVE→AVENUE`; null/blank → `""`.

2. **Required-field validation** (line 177) — `validateRequiredFields` (lines 228-248): collects blank/missing among `firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone` (uses `StringUtils.hasText`), and if any → `throw new MissingOwnerFieldsException(missingFields)` (→ 400). Address is checked *after* normalization.

3. **Postcode validation** (line 178) — `validatePostcode` (lines 262-272): if blank, return (optional); else must match `^[0-9]{4}$` else `InvalidOwnerFieldsException(["postcode"])`; then `OwnerLocality.postcodeMatchesCity(postcode, city)` must be true else `InvalidOwnerFieldsException(["postcode"])` (→ 400).

4. **Map DTO → entity** (line 180) — `ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto)` (section 8).

5. **Telephone normalization** (line 181) — `TelephoneNormalizer.normalize(...)`.
   `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/TelephoneNormalizer.java` (lines 68-94): strip spaces/dashes/brackets; keep leading `+`/country code else assume `+61` and drop one leading `0`; must match `^\+[0-9]{8,15}$` else `InvalidOwnerFieldsException(["telephone"])`; fixed-length national-number check for `+61` (9 digits) and `+1` (10 digits) else `InvalidOwnerFieldsException(["telephone"])` (→ 400).

6. **Email normalization** (line 182) — `normalizeEmail` (lines 357-370): blank → unchanged; else must match `EMAIL_PATTERN` (line 76-77: `^[A-Za-z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Za-z0-9.-]+\.[A-Za-z]{2,}$`) else `InvalidOwnerFieldsException(["email"])`; lowercased; domain checked against `DISPOSABLE_EMAIL_DOMAINS` (lines 86-87: `mailinator.com, tempmail.com, guerrillamail.com`) else `InvalidOwnerFieldsException(["email"])` (→ 400).

7. **Registration-date validation** (line 183) — `validateRegistrationDate` (lines 283-287): if non-null and after `LocalDate.now()` → `InvalidOwnerFieldsException(["registrationDate"])` (→ 400).

8. **Default registration date** (lines 184-186): if null, set to `LocalDate.now()`.

9. **Business-day roll-forward** (line 187) — `toBusinessDay` (lines 445-450): while Sat/Sun, add a day (roll to Monday).

10. **Shares-household flag** (line 188): `Boolean.TRUE.equals(ownerFieldsDto.getSharesHousehold())`.

11. **Household id** (line 189) — `HouseholdNormalizer.householdId(lastName, postcode)`.
    `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/HouseholdNormalizer.java` (lines 53-84): key = normalized(lastName; trim/collapse/lowercase) + `"|"` + (postcode or `""`), SHA-256 hex, first 12 chars.

12. **Identity key** (line 190) — `buildIdentityKey` (lines 316-319): `telephone + "|" + (email or "") + "|" + householdId`.

13. **Household duplicate check** (lines 191-193) — if not sharesHousehold, `rejectHouseholdDuplicate` (lines 298-304): loads `clinicService.findAllOwners()` and if any existing owner has the same `householdId` → `throw new DuplicateOwnerIdentityException(householdId)` (→ 409).

14. **Soft-duplicate detection** (lines 194-196) — `findPossibleDuplicate` (lines 334-346): only if not sharesHousehold and postcode present; finds earliest existing owner with same lastName (case-insensitive) + same postcode + different telephone; sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf`. (Owner is still created.)

15. **City capacity check** (lines 197-199) — `countOwnersInCity` (lines 422-426) via `findAllOwners()`; if `>= CITY_OWNER_LIMIT (50)` → `throw new OwnerCityFullException(city)` (→ 409).

16. **Daily limit check** (lines 200-203) — `countOwnersRegisteredOn` (lines 452-456) via `findAllOwners()`; if `>= DAILY_OWNER_LIMIT (100)` → `throw new OwnerDailyLimitException(registrationDate)` (→ 429).

17. **Bulk-signup warning flag** (line 204): `ownersRegisteredOnDay > BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD (80)` (response flag only).

18. **Customer code** (line 205) — `buildCustomerCode` (lines 380-383): region via `OwnerLocality.forPostcodeAndCity(postcode, city)`, then `CustomerCode.forRegionAndIdentity(region, telephone, lastName)` = `REGION-<first 8 uppercase hex of SHA-256(telephone+lastName)>`.
    `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/CustomerCode.java` (lines 46-49).

19. **Namesake count** (line 206) — `countNamesakes` (lines 394-399): count existing owners with same first+last name (case-insensitive) via `findAllOwners()`.

20. **Household size** (line 207) — `countHouseholdMembers` (lines 409-413) via `findAllOwners()`, `+ 1`.

21. **Persist** (line 208) — `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` (section 4).

22. **Audit log** (lines 209-211) — writes an `AUDIT` logger `info` line including `MembershipLevel.forOwner(owner)` (side-effect: audit logging only; no event published).

23. **Response mapping** (lines 212-216) — `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)`, set `bulkSignupWarning`, set `Location: /api/owners/{id}`, return `201 CREATED`.

Constants: `CITY_OWNER_LIMIT=50` (line 99), `DAILY_OWNER_LIMIT=100` (line 106), `BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD=80` (line 113).

The `OwnerLocality` region/postcode tables live in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerLocality.java` (Sydney→NSW 2000-2099, Melbourne→VIC 3000-3099, Brisbane→QLD 4000-4099; `postcodeMatchesCity` returns true when the city has no known region).

---

## 4. Repository calls

Service facade `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`:

- `findAllOwners()` (lines 126-129, `@Transactional(readOnly = true)`) → `ownerRepository.findAll()`. Called repeatedly by the duplicate/limit/count helpers above (household duplicate, soft-duplicate, city count, daily count, namesake count, household size) — each is a full table scan done in application code, not a DB uniqueness constraint.
- `saveOwner(owner)` (lines 233-237, `@Transactional`) → `ownerRepository.save(owner)`.

Repository interface `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java` (`save` line 76, `findAll` line 84, `findByTelephone` line 58 — the latter is **not** used in the create path).

Active implementation under the `spring-data-jpa` profile: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/springdatajpa/SpringDataOwnerRepository.java` — `@Profile("spring-data-jpa")`, extends Spring Data `Repository`; `save`/`findAll` are Spring Data defaults (insert since id is null). There are also `jpa/JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl.java` and `jdbc/JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl.java` variants for other profiles. **No uniqueness query is issued at save time** — uniqueness is enforced purely by the in-memory `findAll()` scans in section 3.

---

## 5. Security / authorization

- Method-level: `@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")` on `addOwner` (line 173). `@roles` resolves to the Spring bean `Roles`.
  `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/security/Roles.java`: `OWNER_ADMIN = "ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN"` → `hasRole` requires authority `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`.
- Enablement + HTTP security: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/security/BasicAuthenticationConfig.java`: `@EnableMethodSecurity(prePostEnabled = true)` (line 19), `@ConditionalOnProperty(name = "petclinic.security.enable", havingValue = "true")` (line 20) — so `@PreAuthorize` is enforced only when that property is true. `filterChain` requires all requests authenticated with HTTP Basic; CSRF disabled; JDBC-backed users/roles (lines 34-54). A `BCryptPasswordEncoder` bean exists (lines 26-29) but is used for user auth, **not** in the owner-create path.
- `AccessDeniedException` is re-thrown by the advice so Spring Security yields 403 rather than 500 (`ExceptionControllerAdvice.handleAccessDeniedException`, lines 83-86).

---

## 6. Entity lifecycle callbacks / JPA column constraints

Entity `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`:

- `@Entity`, `@Table(name = "owners")` (lines 35-36). **No `@EntityListeners`, no `@PrePersist`/`@PreUpdate`/`@PostPersist`** anywhere in the codebase (verified by search).
- `@Column` mappings carry names only — **no `nullable`/`unique` attributes** on any column. Uniqueness is not enforced at the JPA/DB layer for owners.
